<div class="view on" id="view-home">
  <!-- HOME (task/3445 L3), the console's first page. The owner: "maybe there
       should be an actual homepage that doesnt need much scrolling, just a
       really nice overall dashbaord for the app". So it is headlines only —
       one or two numbers and one plain line per tile, coloured by state —
       and every tile clicks through to the page that holds its detail. He
       reads the TOTALS, never row text, so no tile names a command, a read
       time or an internal subtotal (those are the detail pages' and the hover
       titles'); a reading past its bound says "stale", one never read "not
       read", and every cell boots saying "not read yet", because a dashboard
       that cannot tell ZERO from UNREAD is the defect this console exists to
       kill. -->
  <p id="hello">your projects, remembered</p>
  <!-- ON YOU: what waits on him, one line, and only while something does
       (or while it cannot be read). Its detail — the decisions he answers,
       the asks, the holds — is the On-you block on Work › projects. -->
  <section id="honyou" class="hstrip" data-go="#work/projects">
    <a class="hlab" href="#work/projects">on you</a>
    <span id="honyouline"><span class="hstale">not read</span></span>
  </section>
  <div class="hgrid">
    <section class="htile" data-go="#work/projects">
      <a class="hlab" href="#work/projects">projects</a>
      <div class="hval" id="hprojects"><span class="dmut">not read yet</span></div>
    </section>
    <!-- WORK (task/3643): the Work page's stage row, word for word, and its
         stuck count — one tile where the pipeline and backlog tiles counted
         the same work two ways. -->
    <section class="htile hwide" data-go="#work/work">
      <a class="hlab" href="#work/work" title="every piece of work in every project, from the to-do list to the shared code: the numbers that head the Work page">work</a>
      <div class="hval" id="hwork"><span class="dmut">not read yet</span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="htile" data-go="#quota">
      <a class="hlab" href="#quota">supply</a>
      <div class="hval" id="hsupply"><span class="dmut">not read yet</span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="htile" data-go="#quota">
      <a class="hlab" href="#quota">accounts</a>
      <div class="hval" id="haccounts"><span class="dmut">not read yet</span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="htile" data-go="#roster">
      <a class="hlab" href="#roster" title="seats active right now (a beat in the last 2 minutes), the ones a vendor has walled off, and whether forward work may resume">seats</a>
      <div class="hval" id="hseats"><span class="dmut">not read yet</span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="htile" data-go="#chat">
      <a class="hlab" href="#chat">chat</a>
      <div class="hval" id="hchat"><span class="dmut">not read yet</span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="htile" data-go="#history">
      <a class="hlab" href="#history" title="whether signing is live on the shared record, and how many records the local chain holds and whether they verify">signing record</a>
      <div class="hval" id="hrecord"><span class="dmut">not read yet</span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="htile" data-go="#home" data-open="homenotes">
      <a class="hlab" href="#home">fleet notes</a>
      <div class="hval" id="hnotes"><span class="dmut">not read yet</span></div>
    </section>
    <!-- AWAY MODE (task/3018): the owner's away flag and his notice to every
       agent, set here because he does not type verbs — one line and its
       button, a tile of the grid; why, and the notice, fold under it. Agents
       learn a change at their next turn; nothing here wakes anyone. It boots
       saying "Not read yet", and an unreadable flag is never drawn as
       "here". -->
    <section id="posturesec"></section>
  </div>
  <!-- ANSWERS FOR YOU (owner ruling, task/2364): replies that address HIM,
       from the same reading of the room the push notification path uses. It
       sits directly under the band and ABOVE readiness because it is the one
       thing on this page that is waiting on him rather than reporting to him.
       HIDDEN AT ZERO — chat states emptiness properly, and an empty card here
       is one more thing to look past. It is not an inbox: it holds nothing,
       acknowledges nothing, and reading the room clears it. -->
  <section id="danswers" hidden></section>
  <!-- EVERY FLEET NOTE, folded under the grid: the notes tile carries the
       newest headlines and opens this. -->
  <details class="grp" id="homenotes">
    <summary>every fleet note<span class="gmeta">what the fleet left you</span></summary>
    <!-- FLEET NOTES: the "what happened overnight" answer the fleet leaves
         for you (`helm note set <key> <text>`). Durable, one note per key,
         newest first; the notes tile above carries the newest headlines. -->
    <section id="notesec"></section>
  </details>
  <footer id="foot"></footer>
</div>

